  "mechanism": "Explicit ReadOnlyStatement requests use fresh linearizable quorum selection and an immutable pinned image for already-enrolled Raft SQL databases. They do not append a target command or enrollment. Source-bound requests retain their preceding write proof. SQLite authorizes each read request before stepping. Only explicitly read-only first() and result refusals can stop early; legacy writable prepared statements still drain to completion.",
  "public_contract": [
    "Database::prepare_read_only returns a distinct ReadOnlyStatement with bind, bind_json, all, first and raw. It cannot join a writable batch or session.",
    "One RPC request contains exactly one statement. SQLite rejects writes, transaction control and connection-changing PRAGMAs before execution. Existing protected metadata and parameter, row, byte, cancellation and admission checks remain.",
    "ReadResultSet and ReadMeta omit writer/primary status; a follower can serve the selected image. Cold or undeclared databases are refused without enrollment.",
    "Other durability backends retain owner routing with the same SQLite read-only enforcement. The benchmark SQL read now explicitly selects this API; old recorded algorithms remain distinct."
  ],
